{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "None of these items felt like a strong enough match to choose now. General repair supplies were loosely related to my recent shopping, but they did not meet a specific current need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My repeated interest in framing nails, wood screws and drywall anchors points toward specific fastening tasks; cutting wheels and electrical accessories serve different jobs.",
    "The pipe coupling requires a plumbing task and matching dimensions that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "A caliper could help measure fasteners, but that possible connection does not mean I currently need a precision measuring tool.",
    "Glue could be useful for some repairs, but it does not serve the same purpose as my selected fasteners, and packs of twelve or twenty-four exceed my current needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat tools and repair supplies as broadly interchangeable, even though I choose them for particular tasks.",
    "Buying packages of nails and screws seems to have been taken as interest in bulk supplies generally, although the quantity I need depends on the item and job."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated fastening purchases matter more to my current intent than a loose connection to workshop supplies.",
    "Details such as nail angle, length, shank type, screw size and intended material help determine whether an item would actually fit my task.",
    "My vacuum bag purchase names specific compatible models; household maintenance purchases can reflect an exact replacement need rather than interest in unrelated equipment.",
    "My medicine cup purchase does not establish a need for a non-human infrared thermometer; measuring liquid and measuring surface temperature serve different purposes."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized a broad repair context but missed the specific fastening tasks, compatibility requirements and quantities driving my choices."
}"}
